      "content": "## #TL;DR;\n\n**No code change is needed \u2014 M1 is already fully landed on disk.** I re-read all four files; the management dashboard's `Cost & AI` section already renders the shared `MetricsDashboard`, the inline copy is gone, and the composable no longer exposes the deleted chart computeds. There is **nothing left to patch**.\n\n- \u2705 **`ManagementDashboardView.vue`** \u2014 import present, cost block is `<MetricsDashboard />` in a full-bleed slot, `<main>` is conditional, `sectionReady` short-circuits `cost`, `seriesOptions` / `toggleSeries` are gone, `spendBars` kept.\n- \u2705 **`useManagementDashboard.js`** \u2014 `costChart`, `costByProject`, `costByModel`, `costByPerson`, `budgetByProject`, `projectsForPersonName` are absent from both the body and the returned bag; the `cost` loader, `data.cost`, `fmtCoins`, `fmtNum`, `rangeLabel`, `seriesPath` all survive.\n- \u2705 **`MetricsDashboard.vue` / `appComponentsMap.js`** \u2014 untouched by design; `'analytics'` still maps to `components/analytics/MetricsDashboard.vue`.\n- \u26a0\ufe0f **I cannot run `npm run build`** \u2014 this turn has no shell/command tool, only file content access. The build is the one unmet acceptance criterion and it needs you (command below).\n\n---\n\n## 1. Verification matrix (what the task asked vs. what the files contain)\n\n| Requirement | File | Evidence in current content | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Reuse the existing analytics screen | `ManagementDashboardView.vue` | `import MetricsDashboard from '@/components/analytics/MetricsDashboard.vue'` | \u2705 |\n| Replace the inline cost UI | same | `<div v-else-if=\"d.state.section === 'cost'\" class=\"h-full min-h-0\"><MetricsDashboard /></div>` \u2014 the 6 KPI cards, series toggles, consumption chart, spend-by-project/person, by-model table and budget bars are gone | \u2705 |\n| One header / one scrollbar | same | `<main class=\"flex-1 min-h-0\" :class=\"d.state.section === 'cost' ? 'overflow-hidden p-0' : 'overflow-y-auto p-3 md:p-4'\">` | \u2705 |\n| No skeleton over the embed | same | `case 'cost': return true` in `sectionReady` | \u2705 |\n| Delete chart-only state | same | no `seriesOptions`, no `toggleSeries` in `<script setup>` | \u2705 |\n| Keep Pulse working | same | `spendBars` computed still present and used by the \u201cAI spend trend\u201d card | \u2705 |\n| Remove dead aggregations | `useManagementDashboard.js` | none of `costChart` / `costByProject` / `costByModel` / `costByPerson` / `budgetByProject` / `projectsForPersonName` appear; returned object ends at `memberProjects` / `memberProjectTags` | \u2705 |\n| Keep the cost data path | same | `async cost() { \u2026 }` loader, `data.cost`, consumed by Pulse (`d.data.cost?.total.total_cxjcoins`, `d.data.cost?.budget.pct`, `d.data.cost?.daily`) | \u2705 |\n| Don\u2019t fork the analytics app | `appComponentsMap.js` | `'analytics': lazy(() => import('../components/analytics/MetricsDashboard.vue'))` unchanged | \u2705 |\n\n**One harmless leftover (deliberately not touched, see \u00a74):** `defaultFilters().cost` still carries `series: { cost: true, tokens: false, calls: true }`, dead since the inline chart toggles were removed. It is inert \u2014 `cost()` only reads `filters.cost.project_id` and `.model` \u2014 so removing it would be cosmetic churn, not a fix.\n\n## 2. Why I am not re-writing the files\n\nBoth target files already match the intended end state line for line. Re-emitting a ~900-line composable to delete one unused config key would risk transcription drift (a far worse outcome than an inert key) and violates *\u201cavoid unnecessary changes\u201d*. The change request is satisfied as-is.\n\n## 3. Build & verification steps (needs a shell \u2014 yours)\n\n```\ncd client\nnpm install   # only if node_modules is stale\nnpm run build\n```\n\nWhat a green build proves for this increment:\n1. The `MetricsDashboard` import path resolves.\n2. No template still references a deleted computed (the five symbols are absent from both files, so a failure here would be a genuine regression, not a typo).\n3. `chart.js/auto` + `Collapsible.vue` were already in the bundle via the analytics app \u2192 **no bundle-size jump** expected; if the entry chunk grows, the import landed eagerly somewhere by mistake.\n\nIf it fails, paste the error and the fix is one of: a stale `d.<removed>` reference, or an unused-import lint rule on `MetricsDashboard` (it *is* used, so unlikely).\n\n## 4. Residual gaps (already accepted for M1 / backlog M3)\n\n| Gap | Impact | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| Analytics keeps its **own** header (\u201cAnalytics\u201d + Group by / Admin View / Refresh) under the dashboard header | Cosmetic double header \u2014 visible in the demo | Accepted for M1; a prop (`embedded`/`hideHeader`) is M3 |\n| Analytics keeps its **own** project selector + date presets; the dashboard header\u2019s range/project filter does not reach it | Medium \u2014 management can read a different scope than the header implies | Accepted for M1; M3 passes scope as props |\n| Mount/unmount per visit \u2192 refetch each time | Low (brief spinner) | Accept; `keep-alive` only if it becomes slow |\n| Task board still drops created tasks (`get_task` / `list_tasks` \u2192 not found while `create_task` answers `created`) | Blocks delegation & audit trail | **Needs a human** \u2014 inspect `.codx/tasks/Maintenance/` |\n\n**Recommendation:** run the build, then demo `Cost & AI` and decide M3 (scope props + hide duplicate title) from what management sees.\n\n## 5. Demo script \u2014 5 minutes\n\nOpen the management dashboard \u2192 **Cost & AI**\n1. One header, one scrollbar, no leftover management KPI strip above the screen.\n2. Real totals/tokens/cost; flip **Group by** (minute / hour / day) \u2192 chart follows.\n3. Per-model table shows calls / tokens / cost; **Admin View** reveals per-user and per-project breakdowns.\n4. Open **Price Management**, confirm provider pricing loads; clicking a row\u2019s \u270e prefills the date.\n5. Back to **Pulse** \u2192 \u201cAI spend\u201d KPI and \u201cAI spend trend\u201d bars still show numbers, and both buttons still land on Cost & AI.\n\n## 6. Action taken\n\n| Item | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Read `src/views/ManagementDashboardView.vue` | M1 already applied \u2705 |\n| Read `src/views/management/useManagementDashboard.js` | dead cost aggregations already removed \u2705 |\n| Read `src/components/analytics/MetricsDashboard.vue` | untouched, reusable as-is (Options API, `$el`, own filters) \u2705 |\n| Read `src/config/appComponentsMap.js` | `'analytics'` registration intact \u2705 |\n| Edits produced | **none required** \u2014 a dead `series` key in `defaultFilters().cost` was found and deliberately left (inert; removing it would be churn) |\n| `npm run build` in `client/` | **not executed** \u2014 no shell available in this turn; command and failure-triage in \u00a73 |\n\n**Next step:** run `cd client && npm run build` and report the outcome. If green, M1 is closed and the only open decision is M3 (scope props + duplicate header).",
